.Dd April 14, 2026
.Dt ITHWM 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ithwm
.Nd hardware monitor driver for ITE IT87xx Super I/O chips
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device superio"
.Cd "device ithwm"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes temperature sensors, fan speed counters, and voltage inputs
from the hardware monitor logical device (LDN 4) of ITE IT87xx Super I/O chips
via
.Xr sysctl 8 .
.Pp
To load the driver as a module at boot time, add the following line to
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ithwm_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
Register access uses the 8-byte I/O window provided by the
.Xr superio 4
bus via an index/data port pair.
The driver auto-detects whether the chip operates in 16-bit or 8-bit
tachometer mode from the hardware configuration register.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the following Super I/O hardware monitor chips:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
ITE IT8613E
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following read-only
.Xr sysctl 8
variables are provided under
.Va dev.ithwm.<unit> :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va temp0 , temp1 , temp2
Temperature sensor readings in degrees Celsius, reported using the
.Dq IK
(decikelvin) sysctl format as used by
.Xr amdtemp 4
and
.Xr lm75 4 .
.It Va fan0 , fan1 , fan2
Fan tachometer readings in RPM.
A value of 0 indicates a stalled or absent fan.
.It Va vin0 Ns .. Ns Va vin7
Voltage input readings in millivolts.
Each ADC LSB represents approximately 16 mV.
On-board voltage dividers for higher-voltage rails are board-specific;
raw scaled millivolt values are reported.
.It Va vbat
Battery voltage in millivolts.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr amdtemp 4 ,
.Xr itwd 4 ,
.Xr lm75 4 ,
.Xr superio 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
